# armour/<body>/skirt_split: SPLIT, a coat skirt in two long smooth panels parted at the front: this part is
# the waist over the hips; the panels' tails to the ankle are skirt_split_back (layer back, behind the legs).
# Generated from the FORGE-LIMBS skirt templates (gen_skirts2.py, skirts_def.py; iteration 2: the D view serves U, `tags anyfacing`); Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
# (INTEGRATE silhouettes i2) STARFALL (forge-starfall) gilds the lower edge of the tails facing D and the waist lame's lower row
# facing R and L (its glint cell kept): the T6 hero's trim where the shield hides the front (C12 b).
# Facing R and L at rest and idle the back panel's edge drops one pixel behind the hip, so the tunic hem does not peek
# between the waist lame and the tails (B8: f5_star idle 49 colours).
# (INTEGRATE silhouettes i3) Facing R and L at rest and idle the waist lame has a third, shadowed row one pixel wider
# than the two above: the A3 tunic's hem no longer peeks between the lame and the trousers (C14: teal against purple, 6
# luma apart, on the re-solved FROSTSTEEL), and it reaches the near thigh's front edge, so no 1 px leg sliver is left
# beside it in the walk (B11). Facing L the view's origin moves a column (6 1) for the extra pixel at the back.
use person
body man
role overlay skirt.split
layer hangFront
anchor hip
keys hang
tags anyfacing
z 10

view D key rest origin 9 0
|.vyyyzyyvvxwwwwwv.
|.vxxxxxxvvxwwwwwv.
|vxxxxxv....vwwwwwv
|vyyyyv......vxxxxv
regions
|..NNNNNN..NNNNNN..
|..................
|..................
|.RRRR........RRRR.

